  "summary": "Closed the engineering-owned open findings and the review of the standalone value-type record. DOCX import's post-scope decoding is a documented captured snapshot, proven by a concurrent-import probe. Real-browser paste proof exposed two defects: HTML text blocks containing block images produced schema-invalid slices that insertion dropped, now lifted into sibling blocks by the HTML decoder; and the Plite plain-text fallback threw for anchor blocks needing construction properties, now starting new lines with the default block. DocxImportOptions<true> now requires retainSource: true, correcting the false conditional-typing claim in 2026-09-28-document-conversion-standalone-value-types; compiled type contracts prove editor methods return the editor value and every standalone function returns exactly Value.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "verified",
    "evidence": [
