        "claim": "Final tree: Chromium clipboard 4/4, plitejs 13/13 and 21/21, platejs 90/90, contracts and 141/141, www typecheck with fresh registry and docs parity, Plate Next v245, lint and diff checks pass."
      },
      {
        "path": "apps/www/tests/browser/clipboard.spec.ts",
        "sha256": "3d751d6b2ddb51cf6ad76a8990543ece290ade1d994110ed68f9365497b755ef",
        "claim": "Native and event HTML paste keep safe text around unsafe markup and lift an embedded image without executing handlers."
      },
      {
        "path": "packages/platejs/src/lib/plugins/html/HtmlPlugin.spec.ts",
        "sha256": "b381d6363dcccb2002cfafeb1b391567df78efebd214d06dd6f68d7cf776eb49",
        "claim": "parseHtmlSlice and paste lift a block image out of a paragraph without dropping it."
      },
      {
        "path": "packages/plitejs/test/dom/data-transfer-format.test.ts",
        "sha256": "033eefbec6219f7a9a8fdc1feca38e0ead2a2503a36766d3a975021425b7a72c",
        "claim": "Plain-text fallback over a block with required properties inserts default blocks instead of throwing."
      },
      {
        "path": "packages/platejs/type-tests/standalone-conversion-contracts.ts",
        "sha256": "62ce2241c417007933077a44673663a7236aaef45bc8f96410efb9c91ad22778",
        "claim": "Editor methods return ValueOf of the editor; standalone functions, including server parseHtmlSlice, return exactly Value; retained DOCX options require retainSource: true."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Browser proof is Chromium only; the www Playwright config has no Firefox or WebKit project. Plite slice admission still does not check closed-element content grammar, and insertion can still drop content from such slices for producers other than HTML. Pasting plain text over a range spanning two blocks leaves an empty trailing paragraph. DataTransfer report consumption, Yjs incoming fitting and Markdown streaming cost remain user decisions. Gate receipts live in the gitignored plan artifacts folder. Nothing was committed by this work."
  },
